    description: "Noticed 2026-10-25 during the independent check of WI-tikan: `hypergumbo sketch` on a Django fixture prints a data model as `Author (django django model)`. The concept-derived DataModel label is already '{framework} model' and the sketch formatter prefixes the framework again (sketch.py ~5856, _format_datamodels 5811-5871). Fix: render the framework once (omit the prefix when the label already starts with it, or stop composing the framework into the label). Test on a Django and a Pydantic fixture. Unchecked lead from the same run: `BookSchema(BaseModel)` was labelled '(Schema)' from the naming heuristic, which suggests the Pydantic base-class detector did not fire -- confirm before filing."  # 258d
