  message: "DONE in PR #1869 (merged, dev 7c32fad94c). Root cause: _detect_from_concepts composed the framework into the label ('django model') and sketch's formatter prefixed DataModel.framework again; the formatter's own tests already built label='model', framework='Django', so the producer broke the contract. Fix: the concept label names the construct only; sketch._datamodel_description composes '{framework} {label}' once for grouped AND fallback lines (the fallback used to drop the framework). LIVE REPRO ON MERGED DEV, the item's own shape, production CLI: `hypergumbo sketch` on app/models.py (class Author(models.Model) + class BookSchema(BaseModel)), cold XDG_CACHE_HOME -> rc 0, 'Author (django model)' (was 'Author (django django model)'). Test: test_sketch.py::TestFormatDatamodels::test_concept_model_names_its_framework_once (detect_datamodels -> _format_datamodels, grouped + fallback) and test_datamodels.py::test_label_does_not_repeat_the_framework[model|schema|entity]. The item's unchecked Pydantic lead is CONFIRMED and filed separately as WI-kiluh: BookSchema still reads '(Schema)' because the base-class detector reads meta parent_bases, which no analyzer emits."  # 84d4
